Subject: A Few Questions from a Newbie about Getting Started with devtools
Message-ID: <zk-biarAj_o.qTiCaplPDQAJ@rdevtools.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rdevtools/c/zk-biarAj_o/m/qTiCaplPDQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I consider myself a novice to intermediate R programmer and have a few good ideas for libraries that I would move forward with. I am a newbie in terms of developing libraries and I have no experience building R libraries but would like to get that understanding. I have pretty much no experience with GitHub but I do have an account. I have devtools installed. My first question is, how to initialize a new project and can devtools automatically create a GitHub repository under my user name and install the correct directory structure there. I am guessing that this is the case because of the install_github() command in devtools although I'm not sure. Can somebody provide with some clear insight how to "sync my application from my computer with my GitHub repository", also can somebody please explain the idea of pull request?

